{
	title: 'Changes window over the web app',
	spec: "A session's file changes show in a native modal dialog over the web app at /<session id>/changes; ?path=<encoded absolute path> selects one recorded file. Loading that address opens the app on that tab with the window open; the old /changes/<id> address redirects there, keeping its query, so older links keep working. Links to it (status details, /changes output, the context page) use the new address; on the web, following one for the shown tab opens the window in place without a page load, closing other open dialogs. Escape, the close button or a click outside closes it and the address returns to /<id>. Choosing a file rewrites ?path= without a new history entry. Wide screens show the file list beside the selected file's diff (the first file when none is named); narrow screens show the list, then the chosen file with a way back. The window is neutral like the transcript (the plain style: gray text, near-white file names, darker gray secondary text and lines), not the amber page colors; only the diff and its counts are colored. The picker dialogs (model, /config, find) and Session details use the same neutral colors and one frame: a 44px header bar (title, close button) under a line, a soft shadow, a short opacity fade in and out, and actions in a footer above a line, as full 44px buttons (Session details: Log out this browser). Each row shows the path, colored +added -removed, local time and linked block ids. The file pane shows the commit label, other sessions observing the same path, the unified diff without Git header lines, with old and new line numbers, additions and removals in the diff colors and hunk headers faint, then foldable steps per call when two or more calls changed it. Up/Down (or k/j) move between files. Data comes from GET /<id>/changes.json (the list) and ?path= (one file in full): authenticated, read-only, no-store, the same selection rule (only recorded paths; others 404) and non-blocking history catch-up as before. Fetch failures show their status and body in the window.",
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Implementation: host/changes-page.ts serves the JSON and the /changes/<id> redirect; web/changes.ts holds the address (router.changes, changesHref) and diff-line parsing; components/Changes.tsx is the dialog, intercepting plain clicks on same-origin links for the shown tab (a /<id>#tN card link while open pushes that address and calls app.aim, so Back reopens the window). router.parse accepts /<id>/changes; router.go drops ?path when switching tabs. The list endpoint computes each file diff for counts but omits the text; commit labels, neighbors and steps load only for the selected file. Checked by hand in headless Chrome at 1400 and 390 px wide: open by address, file selection, close, in-page reopen, ArrowDown and Escape.'
